---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const features=[['Ask','Read-only questions grounded in files, selections, diagnostics and workspace code.'],['Plan','Inspect the architecture and create an implementation plan before changing code.'],['Agent','Prepare multi-file proposals, review diffs, validate approved edits and attempt repairs.'],['Your compute','Use local Ollama, configured OpenAI-compatible endpoints, or your own remote Ollama GPU over SSH.'],['Reviewed changes','Snapshot checks and atomic proposals help prevent stale changes from being applied.'],['Model management','Discover models, choose providers, and manage local downloads inside the extension.']];
---
<Layout title="LOMVREN | Local-first AI Engineering by Ganesh Naidu" description="LOMVREN, formerly LocalForge, is a local-first VS Code coding assistant with Ask, Plan, Agent, reviewed edits and remote GPU inference over SSH." path="/lomvren/"><section class="wrap page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">PRODUCT / FORMERLY LOCALFORGE</div><h1>Meet <em>LOMVREN.</em><br/>Build with your own AI.</h1><p class="lead">A local-first autonomous engineering environment inside VS Code. Keep your model choice, compute and development workflow in your hands.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button dark" href="https://github.com/paladuguganeshnaidu/LocalForge">Explore the repository ↗</a><a class="button" href="https://github.com/paladuguganeshnaidu/LocalForge#Getting-Started">Getting started ↗</a></div><p class="small">Active development · Product name and capabilities follow the public repository.</p></section><section class="wrap section"><div class="grid">{features.map(([title,desc])=><article class="card" data-reveal><div class="meta">LOMVREN</div><h2>{title}</h2><p>{desc}</p></article>)}</div></section><section class="wrap section"><div class="callout"><h2>Local first. Explicit destinations.</h2><p>Local inference uses your configured runtime. Remote SSH mode sends prompts and included context to your selected host; API mode sends them to your configured endpoint. The extension does not operate a hosted inference service.</p><p>Terminal commands run with your existing account permissions. Reviewed file proposals and command approvals are part of the workflow; they do not provide an operating-system sandbox.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/paladuguganeshnaidu/LocalForge#security--privacy-architecture">Read the product architecture ↗</a></div></section></Layout>